      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors described a case of the patient of the idiopatic group of PVT. Due to only a few symptoms, the diagnosis was established late. This was confirmed by the fact, that the patient was not hospitalized. So it was an atypical case of chronic PVT. Portal vein thrombosis belongs to rare clinical conditions. Early diagnosis based on modern technique is possible only if we keep this condition in mind (Tab. 1, Fig. 1, Ref. 23)."},
